Releasing mvm05a.  Void is now based on only the items used, rather
than all items carried.  I left a preprocessor macro (MONK_VOID_CARRY)
in, if you prefer micromanaging your inventory.  This removes the huge
emphasis on controlling what you carry and how you carry it.  It gives
a benefit to early monks, who have less opportunity to fill up their
use-slots, while penalizing monks which have built up a large
collection of constantly-used objects.  I find it more fun to play
than my earlier versions. :)

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#mvm

DETAIL SPOILER:

I gave up trying to find all the places where inventory and usage
changes, and just recalc'd monkvoid and printed the bottom lines once
per player turn loop.

monkvoid doesn't instantly jump from one value to another: instead, it
drifts by one point, if needed, each time set_monkvoid is called.

Since it's not an inventory-micromanaging patch any more, I only offer
a sack to the starting monk if MONK_VOID_CARRY is defined.

